      },
      "description": "p95 of each RAG query stage over the last hour: embedding the query through the gateway, searching the Qdrant collections, which run at once so the stage takes as long as the slower search, and ranking the results locally. Each line is its own quantile, so the stages' p95 need not add up to the whole query's. Approximate: increase() needs two samples of a series inside its window, so a series' first sample, and any series seen only once in the window, add nothing, and delta points from one process can arrive out of order (#792). The counts lost can fall in any bucket, so a quantile can come out high or low.",
